Subject: Replace bundled xmlParser (AFPL) with pugixml (MIT) via xml_compat wrapper
Author:  Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>
Origin:  Local morpheus fork — memory/morpheus_xmlparser_replacement.md

Wraps morpheus's small subset of xmlParser usage (XMLNode, XMLResults,
XMLError, XMLAttribute, XMLClear, XMLParserBase64Tool) on top of system
pugixml (MIT-licensed, in Fedora). Replaces the AFPL-licensed xmlParser
bundle, which Fedora cannot ship. Generated from a diff of vanilla
morpheus-2.3.9 against the same tree with the wrapper applied, so the
patch is byte-exact and applies under `patch --fuzz=0` (the strict
default mock/rpmbuild uses).

--- a/3rdparty/CMakeLists.txt	2025-02-28 03:17:39.000000000 -0800
+++ b/3rdparty/CMakeLists.txt	2026-05-24 22:12:00.478037562 -0700
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 add_subdirectory(muParser)
-add_subdirectory(xmlParser)
+# xmlParser removed — replaced by pugixml via xml_compat wrapper (AFPL -> MIT license)
 add_subdirectory(tiny-process)
 add_subdirectory(gnuplot_i)
 SET(XTENSOR_USE_XSIMD 1)
